    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "What is a Life Page?",
      "Anchor": "what-is-a-life-page",
      "SectionPath": [
        "What is a Life Page?"
      ],
      "Text": "A Life Page (also known as a \u0022Life at [Company]\u0022 page) is a customizable section of a LinkedIn Company Page where organizations showcase their company culture, values, and employee experiences to attract potential talent. Admins can create multiple targeted versions of their Life Page, each with content tailored to specific audiences based on attributes such as location, industry, job function, and seniority.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "What is a Life Page?",
      "Anchor": "what-is-a-life-page",
      "SectionPath": [
        "What is a Life Page?"
      ],
      "Text": "Life Pages can include:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "What is a Life Page?",
      "Anchor": "what-is-a-life-page",
      "SectionPath": [
        "What is a Life Page?"
      ],
      "Text": "Featured leaders and recruiters\nCustom media sections with images and videos\nEmployee testimonials\nPhotos showcasing company culture\nEmployee-generated content tagged with specific hashtags\nContact information for interested candidates",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "What is a Life Page?",
      "Anchor": "what-is-a-life-page",
      "SectionPath": [
        "What is a Life Page?"
      ],
      "Text": "To view a Life Page on LinkedIn, navigate to a company page and click on the \u0022Life\u0022 tab.\nExample: linkedin.com/company/[company-name]/life/",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Feature Overview",
      "Anchor": "feature-overview",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Feature Overview"
      ],
      "Text": "The Organization Life Page Traffic Statistics API returns page view and visitor traffic statistics for Life Pages (Targeted Content pages) on LinkedIn. This API helps admins understand how many people are viewing their Life Page content and track engagement across different targeted content variations.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Feature Overview",
      "Anchor": "feature-overview",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Feature Overview"
      ],
      "Text": "Each Life Page variation has a unique reportingId used to track and report on its traffic statistics. This API allows you to retrieve traffic data for one or more Life Page variations by providing their reporting IDs.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Feature Overview",
      "Anchor": "feature-overview",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Feature Overview"
      ],
      "Text": "Tip",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Feature Overview",
      "Anchor": "feature-overview",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Feature Overview"
      ],
      "Text": "How to determine which organizational pages you can query?\nTo find organizations you can query traffic statistics for, use OrganizationAuthorization\u0027s BATCH_FIND by AuthorizationAction and AuthenticatedMember with the authorization action set to CareerPageAuthorizationActionType.CAREER_PAGE_LIFE_READ.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How to Obtain Reporting IDs",
      "Anchor": "how-to-obtain-reporting-ids",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Obtain Reporting IDs"
      ],
      "Text": "Before you can query traffic statistics, you need to obtain the reportingId values for your Life Page content. Follow these steps:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How to Obtain Reporting IDs",
      "Anchor": "how-to-obtain-reporting-ids",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Obtain Reporting IDs"
      ],
      "Text": "Verify Authorization: Ensure the authenticated member has the required role on the organization. Use OrganizationAuthorization\u0027s BATCH_FIND with authorizationAction:(organizationAnalyticsAuthorizationAction:(actionType:CAREER_PAGE_LIFE_READ)) to verify access.\n\nFetch Targeted Content: Use the Organization Targeted Contents API to retrieve all Life Page variations for your organization.\nExample:\n Copy GET /rest/organizationTargetedContents?q=organization\u0026organization={ORGANIZATION_URN}\n\n\nExtract Reporting IDs: Each targeted content item in the response will contain a reportingId field. These are the unique identifiers you\u0027ll use to query traffic statistics.\n\nQuery Traffic Statistics: Once you have the reporting IDs, pass them to this API as shown in the examples below.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How to Obtain Reporting IDs",
      "Anchor": "how-to-obtain-reporting-ids",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Obtain Reporting IDs"
      ],
      "Text": "The service currently provides the following methods:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How to Obtain Reporting IDs",
      "Anchor": "how-to-obtain-reporting-ids",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Obtain Reporting IDs"
      ],
      "Text": "Organization - Fetches the life page traffic statistics for a given organization using reporting IDs.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
